# Unity AR Rules

- Target Unity 6.6 and Android ARCore via AR Foundation.
- Use meters for all spatial measurements.
- Treat ARCore plane and depth estimates as uncertain input, not ground truth.
- Separate AR tracking / session coordinates from persisted room geometry.
- Do not treat detected plane boundaries as accurate walls.
- Prefer a room model that can be manually corrected after scan.
- Keep geometry generation testable in the Unity Editor with mock data.
- Preserve all Unity `.meta` files.
- Report Editor tests and device/ARCore tests separately.
- Leave `native-ai/` alone; consume only documented contracts.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: persist live AR session poses as room truth
room.Save(arPlane.transform.position);

// ✅ GOOD: convert to room-local meters, then persist
room.Save(ToRoomLocalMeters(arPlane));
```
